      "n_units": 49,
      "verification": "Checked by hand on 2026-11-04 against the file, DANDI 001880's metadata and the paper (Huszár et al. 2026, Neuron, the author manuscript on PubMed Central, PMC13573635, whose Data availability names this dandiset). Units: 49 (26 CA1, 23 CA3; 28 'Pyramidal Cell', 14 'Narrow Interneuron', 7 'Wide Interneuron'; 12 CA1- and 10 CA3-opto-tagged). Time: 236,084 position samples every 0.03335 s (29.99 Hz; the paper states a 30 Hz camera) from 64.27 to 17,300.79 s, inside the PRE, Learning and POST sub-sessions, with Rest 1 and Rest 2 untracked between them; spikes from 0.006 to 19,540.87 s, inside the file's sleep scoring (1 to 19,539 s, the last spike 1.9 s after it) and the opto-tagging light pulses (17,336 to 19,497 s) after the last position sample. Space: positions in cm by the series' unit, 5.3% NaN; the samples tracked during onMaze span 90.7 x 89.6 cm against the paper's 90 cm platform, 5.7% of them beyond its radius from their midrange. Events: 2,118 ripples, 195 inside an onMaze row; 45 learning trials with both rewards; at each of the 90 reward times the tracked position lies a median 2.34 cm from the rewardCoordinates row its rewardOrder names (43.5 cm from the other). Tracking: 90 runs of 11 or more identical samples (29.1% of the frames, the longest 81.7 s); 95% of the tracked samples outside onMaze repeat the one before, a median 44.3 cm from the disc's centre. The overview figure and frames of rec.animation() (Matplotlib) were looked at: the path covers the disc, the held fixes pile up at its east edge, the reward wells sit on the path, and the scene shows the mouse on the maze with the wells, the raster and the on_maze, open_box, pre and awake epochs."
    },
